            <div xml:id="d973">

                <pb facs="1232" n="1218" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/8–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-04T19:00:00-04:00">September 4,
                            1945—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. Reurtel 471, Aug. 29. Please say to President Somoza that while Dept
                    appreciates his suggestion that you and Dept join him in considering the proper
                    person to receive Nicaraguan Presidential <pb facs="1233" n="1219"
                        xml:id="pg1219"/> nomination nevertheless Dept considers selection of
                    candidates is a part of the electoral process and could best be left to internal
                    decision in Nicaragua in accordance constitutional mandates and provisions
                    electoral laws.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
